cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, cite it as below."
title: "Kelvins Collision Avoidance Study: threshold-explicit evaluation of collision-probability forecasts"
abstract: >-
  A reproduction of the ESA Kelvins Spacecraft Collision Avoidance Challenge
  baseline (F2 = 0.7391 against a published 0.739), with the orbital, covariance
  and probability-of-collision layers rebuilt and validated against NASA CARA's
  own Pc code, and an evaluation layer measuring false positives and false
  negatives at five operator reaction thresholds over 199,082 CDMs.
